      {
        "number": 3,
        "instructionsHtml": "Part 3<p>Listen and answer questions 21–30.</p>",
        "groups": [
          {
            "id": "part-3-group-1",
            "type": "mcq",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 21–24</h3><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p><p><strong>Assignment on sleep and dreams</strong></p>",
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 21,
                "textHtml": "Luke read that one reason why we often forget dreams is that",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "our memories cannot cope with too much information."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "we might otherwise be confused about what is real."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "we do not think they are important."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 22,
                "textHtml": "What do Luke and Susie agree about dreams predicting the future?",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "It may just be due to chance."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "It only happens with certain types of event."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "It happens more often than some people think."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 23,
                "textHtml": "Susie says that a study on pre-school children having a short nap in the day",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "had controversial results."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "used faulty research methodology."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "failed to reach any clear conclusions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 24,
                "textHtml": "In their last assignment, both students had problems with",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "statistical analysis."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "making an action plan."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "self-assessment."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "part-3-group-2",
            "type": "completion",
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 25–30</h3><p>Complete the flow chart below.</p><p>Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p>",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "maxWords": 1,
            "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-title\">Assignment plan</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Decide on research question: Is there a relationship between hours of sleep and number of dreams?</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Decide on sample: Twelve students from the {{25}} department</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Decide on methodology: Self-reporting</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Decide on procedure: Answers on {{26}}</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Check ethical guidelines for working with {{27}}. Ensure that risk is assessed and {{28}} is kept to a minimum</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">Analyse the results: Calculate the correlation and make a {{29}}</div>\n<div class=\"flow-arrow\">↓</div>\n<div class=\"flow-box\">{{30}} the research</div></div>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "number": 4,
        "instructionsHtml": "Part 4<p>Listen and answer questions 31–40.</p>",
        "groups": [
          {
            "id": "part-4-group-1",
            "type": "completion",
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 31–40</h3><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p>",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "maxWords": 1,
            "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-title\">Health benefits of dance</div>\n<p class=\"sub-head\">Recent findings:</p>\n<ul class=\"notes-list\">\n<li>All forms of dance produce various hormones associated with feelings of happiness.</li>\n<li>Dancing with others has a more positive impact than dancing alone.</li>\n<li>An experiment on university students suggested that dance increases {{31}}.</li>\n<li>For those with mental illness, dance could be used as a form of {{32}}.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"sub-head\">Benefits of dance for older people:</p>\n<ul class=\"notes-list\">\n<li>accessible for people with low levels of {{33}}</li>\n<li>reduces the risk of heart disease</li>\n<li>better {{34}} reduces the risk of accidents</li>\n<li>improves {{35}} function by making it work faster</li>\n<li>improves participants' general well-being</li>\n<li>gives people more {{36}} to take exercise</li>\n<li>can lessen the feeling of {{37}}, very common in older people</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"sub-head\">Benefits of Zumba:</p>\n<ul class=\"notes-list\">\n<li>A study at The University of Wisconsin showed that doing Zumba for 40 minutes uses up as many {{38}} as other quite intense forms of exercise.</li>\n<li>The <em>American Journal of Health Behavior</em> study showed that:\n<ul><li>women suffering from {{39}} benefited from doing Zumba.</li>\n<li>Zumba became a {{40}} for the participants.</li></ul></li>\n</ul></div>"
          }
        ]
      }
